Agent Vigil is a defensive security and change-control utility for AI coding agents.

Its dual-use capabilities include parsing agent transcripts and tool commands,
evaluating repository changes against authorization and integrity policies,
running maintainer-configured verification commands and isolated upgrade
canaries, and producing evidence about blocked or permitted actions. These
capabilities can inspect or execute user-supplied commands and can be repurposed
outside their intended defensive context.

Agent Vigil is intended for repository owners and maintainers to review agent
behavior, enforce change-control boundaries, test upgrades, and create
verifiable receipts for their own systems. It does not grant authorization to
access or modify third-party systems. Use it only on systems and repositories
you own or are explicitly authorized to assess.
